{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"- **Sponsor economics:** Estimate actual advisory revenue after waivers and expense reimbursements—not simply AUM × the published expense ratio. Compare it with operating, distribution, seed-financing and liquidity-support costs. Assess break-even AUM, cash-burn runway, sponsor financial strength, waiver expiration/recoupment terms, and whether a larger platform subsidizes the fund. Strategic importance may justify prolonged losses.\n\n- **Seed durability:** Identify who economically owns the seed, its concentration, compensation arrangements, redemption rights, lockups and exit incentives. Distinguish committed investment capital from temporary launch capital or market-maker inventory. A large seed position can mask weak independent demand and create a redemption cliff.\n\n- **Replacement demand:** Track outside-investor assets, organic net flows excluding seed movements, investor diversification and distribution progress. Market appreciation alone does not demonstrate commercial traction.\n\n**Worth knowing:** There is no universal closure-AUM threshold; sponsor willingness and ability to fund losses matter alongside asset size."}}
